+## Context
+
+`createTask`, `renameTask` and `addTag` in `task.ts` are pure and cannot fail; `list.ts` composes them. Results are used for errors in the domain.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Add `invalid-input` to `TodoErrorCode`: none of the existing codes fits.
+- Put the checks in `task.ts` as small helpers (`validateTitle`, `validatePriority`, `validateTag`) returning `Result`; `renameTask` and `addTag` now return `Result<Task>`; `createTask` stays infallible and `list.add` calls `validateNewTask` first.
+- In `list.ts`, `add` validates before issuing an id, so a rejection consumes no id; `rename` validates before the duplicate check; `tag` goes through `change` and returns the error unchanged.
+- Title length is measured on the trimmed title, in JS string length.
+- Domain stays pure: no clock, no randomness, no throwing, no dependency. The public API gets no new function.
+
+## Risks
+
+- `createTask`, `renameTask`, `addTag` are not exported from `src/index.ts`, so changing their return type does not affect the app.
