+## Why
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, so odd tasks get in: blank titles, huge titles, unknown priorities, tags with spaces. The list should reject them with a clear error.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `add`, `rename` and `tag` validate their input and fail with a new error code `invalid-input` and a message saying what is wrong.
+- Rules: title not empty or only spaces; title at most 120 characters (after trimming); priority one of `low`, `normal`, `high`; tag not empty and without a space. On `add`, the tags given are checked too.
+- A rejected call changes nothing in the list (no task added, renamed or tagged, no id used).
+- `TodoErrorCode` gains `invalid-input`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-input-validation`: what input the list accepts for titles, priorities and tags, and how it rejects the rest.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Project rules touched: errors are returned as a `Result` in the domain (validation returns `err`, never throws); TSDoc on every new exported function; no clock or randomness added; no new dependency. A code is added to `result.ts` because none of the existing codes fits.
+- Public API in `src/index.ts`: no new export, but the exported `TodoErrorCode` type gains `'invalid-input'`.
+- Code: `src/domain/result.ts`, `src/domain/task.ts` (`renameTask`, `addTag` now return `Result`), `src/domain/list.ts`, `test/list.test.ts`.
